{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Jethro heard</b> Our Rabbis said: he heard the splitting of the Sea of Reeds — for when the sea split, it let out a great roar until all the kings of east and west heard it. This is what is written: «and it shall roar over him… like the roaring of the sea.» They also said: he heard the war of Amalek." "<b>And Jethro heard, priest of Midian, father-in-law</b> — in gematria: אלה הם קריעת הים ומלחמת עמלק («these are the splitting of the sea and the war of Amalek»). יתרו in gematria = כומר — he was a priest of idolatry — and in gematria = התורה. He came to convert and to receive the Torah. In the language of the RI\"A, the Rosh, z\"l: יתרו — read it יתר ו׳ («extra vav»), for he had six names, extra beyond the rest of mankind. Another interpretation: he came to receive the Ten Commandments and תר״ו (606) commandments, extra beyond the seven [Noahide] commandments with which the children of Noah were commanded: «all that Elohim had done for Moses.»" "<b>Why does it say Elohim?</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, made Moses an אלהים («a god / judge») over Pharaoh — that is, a prince. Alternatively: he heard that He came upon him with the attribute of judgment to kill him, for he had not circumcised his son, as it says: «and HaShem met him and sought to put him to death» — and he heard that he was saved from this." "<b>עשה אלהים</b> — Two times in the Masorah: here and the other in the portion of Miketz: «What is this that Elohim has done to us?» — with the same expression by which they were distressed, with that same expression they gained profit upon their departure from there."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The scriptural quotation «וינהום עליו וגו' כנהמת ים» is left unaddressed as it appears; it alludes to Isaiah 5:30, not identified by the author.", 1 "The abbreviation א\"א (אחי אבי / אח אבי) likely refers to a paternal uncle; resolved following common Ba'al HaTurim usage.", 2 "The cryptic «פי׳ א» likely abbreviates «פירוש אחד» («one explanation»); resolved with uncertainty."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:36.418997058Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}